# WHY EVERY ENTRY BELOW CARRIES AN EXPLICIT `=<40-hex sha>`
#
# `clone-siblings` resolves a BARE entry from the workspace lock, and raises
# NEED_LOCK for it -- which makes a missing lock FATAL. No lock is published
# for this repo's branch tip, so every reprobuild run died in `clone-siblings`
# with:
#
#     ::error::No workspace lock for ngx-isonim (candidates: ...). Neither a
#     repo-workspaces locks/<project>/ngx-isonim/<sha>.xml nor a reprobuild
#     locks/<project>/ngx-isonim/<sha>.toml exists in
#     metacraft-labs/metacraft-manifests@latest.
#
# before a single dependency was provisioned. With no bare entry left, nothing
# needs a revision FROM the lock, so `lock_unavailable()` degrades to a
# `::warning::` and the clones proceed.
#
# Each SHA below is the tip of the ref that sibling's own repository actually
# uses as its default branch, verified to exist with `git ls-remote` (the refs
# are NOT uniformly `main` -- see the `@<branch>` note on each line).
#
# THIS IS THE FALLBACK, NOT THE GOAL. `clone-siblings.sh` prescribes it in
# that order: (1) declare these repos in ngx-isonim's project manifest in
# metacraft-labs/metacraft-manifests so the lock pins them for every future
# commit with nothing to maintain; (2) only where (1) is impossible, name a
# 40-hex commit SHA here -- a commit, never a branch, because a branch tip is
# exactly the unpinned resolve the mechanism exists to prevent. Delete these
# `=<sha>` suffixes as soon as (1) lands.
#
# Cross-repo siblings cloned by setup-dev-env at the explicit SHAs
# pinned below (see codetracer-specs/Testing/Cross-Repo-CI-Integration.md).
#
# Since IFP-M2 (isonim_rpc) the module and its mock tests import IsoNim's
# request, response, request-context and server-function modules
# (isonim/src/isonim/server/{request,response,context,rpc}.nim), and since
# IFP-M3 it serves IsoNim's hydration bootstrap (generateHydrationScript of
# isonim/src/isonim/ssr/markers.nim). Since then it also imports
# isonim/server/response_body and the writer's unsentBytes.
#
# These two SHAs MUST equal the `isonim` and `nim-everywhere` revisions in
# repro.lock and flake.lock: `just test` and `just test-e2e` compile against
# these clones, `nix build .#module` against the flake inputs. A pin moved in
# the locks but not here builds CI against a different isonim than the one
# every commit message reports verified (at bd31893 `just test` failed with
# "cannot open file: isonim/server/response_body"). nim-everywhere is the
# revision this isonim pins.
isonim=2f4a6dba3bc2eca2d00d5448bf1a8d9d2ab4f49e  # isonim@agents (unsentBytes, streaming data entries)
nim-everywhere=2a41b67a6c0d41cbb55359c702f300eb2696682f  # the revision isonim 2f4a6dba pins
# scripts/build-module.sh compiles the module against ../nim-faststreams and
# ../nim-stew (its DEFAULT_PATHS), so `just build` and `just test-e2e`
# (.github/workflows/e2e.yml) need them on disk. The same revisions isonim's
# own .github/sibling-repos pins (see its notes on both).
nim-faststreams=82c8c3edb5fa7a4fdfcdb5d8ab53bbe1830d4503
nim-stew=83eb1157963b7f49351dbdd858355fa990bbe23c
